 about the number of new  cases we repeat the numbers of people  who have died  with quote a positive covert 19 19 tests  we'd quite like to provide some accurate  information daily information  on how many people are getting  vaccinated because frankly that seems  like one of the few good news stories  around at the moment  could we get that information from your  department on a daily basis  well we publish it weekly at the moment  and yeah we've been  we've been working so hard with the nhs  doing such a brilliant job to get this  up and running at pace we've obviously  delivered more than a million  vaccines into arms already that's more  than the rest of europe  put together i'm really proud of how the  nhs have really risen to this challenge  from today we accelerate that path  we've got from today 700 vaccination  sites open across the uk  by the end of the week it's due to be  over a thousand  uh so the there's plenty of statistics i  can keep going  i'm really really pleased and and the  whole of the nhs is is leading into this  incredibly important national effort  and it it's only because right at the  start  we saw that the vaccine was the only way  out  long term we backed the the scientists  at  oxford and we teamed them up with  astrazeneca who themselves are doing a  great job and now we have this big  british success story  starting today but we will see in a few  we'll have to leave a few weeks until we  get to the point of saying that we've  got the vaccination program going quite  as quite as you'd like and  you know daily information would help us  in assessing that but just in terms of  the vaccines a huge amount of concern  about a change to the protocol the  distance between the first  and the second doses explain this one to  us because  there are plenty of people who suggest  well i took that first vaccine  on the promise that i would get the  second one as scheduled  why is that not happening and how  concerned should people be it's  it's 